.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n\n- At 304 PM MDT, Doppler radar indicated heavy rain due to\nthunderstorms. Minor flooding is ongoing or expected to begin\nshortly in the advisory area.\n\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nMainly rural areas of Central Larimer County.","ends":"2026-08-26T18:00:00-06:00","severity":"Minor","areaDesc":"Larimer, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.6be35616492a811ce0f7cf1195998ae24ec9cbf0.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.6be35616492a811ce0f7cf1195998ae24ec9cbf0.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"BOU","issued":"2026-08-26T17:40:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KBOU 261740 AFDBOU Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Denver/Boulder CO 1140 AM MDT Wed Aug 26 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Scattered afternoon/evening thunderstorms expected for theI-25 Corridor and plains. A few storms could become severe, with large hail and strong winds possible. - Thunderstorm coverage decreases Thursday and Friday with mainly isolated high-based showers/","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=BOU&issuedby=BOU&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":null,"fwf":{"office":"BOU","issued":"2026-08-26T20:23:00+00:00","snippet":".DISCUSSION...Rest of today through Thursday...Scattered thunderstorms will move across the urban corridor and eastern plains late this afternoon and early evening with heavy rain, hail, and strong winds. Warmer and drier air moves in for Thursday with isolated high-based showers/thunderstorms. Gusty outflow winds will accompany the showers/thunderstorms while any rainfall will be light. LONG TERM","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=BOU&issuedby=BOU&product=FWF&format=CI"},"coagmet":{"station_id":"fcl01","station_name":"Fort Collins","distance_km":19.9,"soil_temp_5cm_f":-999,"soil_temp_15cm_f":74.75,"soil_moisture_5cm":null,"soil_moisture_15cm":null,"precip_in":null,"eto_in":null,"vapor_pressure":null,"solar_radiation":465.6,"wind_speed_mph":3.82,"air_temp_f":82.6